    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d404">

                <pb facs="0744" n="650" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg650"/>

                <head>No. 404.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Baron Fava.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 3,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Baron</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt oil your note of the 1st instant, announcing that Italy, now at war with
                    Abyssinia, has established a blockade of the coast of that power from Amphylla
                        <pb facs="0745" n="651" xml:id="pg651"/> to a point opposite the Island of
                    Dufnein, and that the prize court will eventually sit at Massana.</p>
                <p>Publicity is given to the announcement to the end that all whom it may concern
                    may take cognizance of such effective blockade as maybe maintained upon the
                    coast in question by the naval forces of Italy.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
